WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.467
A U.S.

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:01.301
official tells CNN

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.002
that a Russian jet

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.304
intentionally flew in front of the UN

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.374
in front of the unmanned U.S.

00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:09.609
Reaper drone, such as the one seen here

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.679
And then the Russians dumped jet

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.280
fuel in front of it

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.982
and then damaged a propeller

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.684
on the drone, which forced the U.S.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.953
Air Force to then bring the drone down.

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:22.022
We're covering this from the Pentagon,

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.290
from the White House and in Ukraine.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.291
Let's start with CNN's Oren

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.493
Liebermann at the Pentagon for us.

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:27.660
And Oren, U.S.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.195
aircraft flying over the black seas,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:31.431
international waters not uncommon.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:32.432
Is it clear

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.433
whether or not the Russians

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.402
did this intentionally?

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.603
Jake, the Pentagon and the U.S.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.071
military have been very careful

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.440
not to ascribe an intent or goal

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.941
to the Russian pilots inside

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.143
those two Russian aircrafts.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.010
But it's also very clear

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.678
that if you look at the description

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.613
of how this played out,

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.448
it certainly looks, at least in part,

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.282
deliberate

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:49.783
The Pentagon

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.583
says over the course of

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.552
about 30 to 40 minutes,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.787
two of these Russian

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:55.321
su 27 fighter jets

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.391
repeatedly flew in front of sprayed fuel

00:00:58.391 --> 00:00:59.192
in front of

00:00:59.192 --> 00:00:59.959
and then ultimately

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.828
one of them collided with this

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.096
MQ nine Reaper

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:04.464
drone, damaging the propeller

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.265
and forcing the U.S.

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.533
to bring down the drone

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.967
over international waters.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:08.635
It should be noted that

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:09.636
all of this played out

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:11.004
over international waters,

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.138
according to the US.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.173
Russia firing back

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.340
just a short time ago,

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.643
saying they did not use airborne weapons

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:18.178
or come into contact

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.013
with the MQ nine Reaper drone.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.381
The Pentagon has said, however,

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.482
that there is video

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.049
that they're working

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.017
to put out, imagery

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:25.185
that they're working to put out,

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:25.919
which will certainly paint

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.054
a clearer picture of how this played out.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.588
But Jake,

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.490
repeatedly crossing in front of a U.S.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.091
drone

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:33.093
over the course of 30 to 40 minutes,

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.928
whether you meant to hit it or not.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.362
That sort of interaction comes

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:38.431
across as very intentional

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:38.832
to us,

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.467
calling this unsafe, unprofessional,

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.669
even going so far as to call it reckless.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:44.003
And let's bring in our Ivan Watson,

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:45.772
who is in eastern Ukraine for us.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.439
Ivan,

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.841
anything more you can tell us about

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:49.476
what the Kremlin is saying

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.276
about this incident?

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:53.279
Sure.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.782
I mean, the Russian Ministry of Defense

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.283
issued its statement

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.384
within the last hour,

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.420
basically confirming that, yes, in fact,

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:01.588
something had happened

00:02:01.588 --> 00:02:03.089
there that resulted in the loss

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.158
of this U.S. Air Force Reaper.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.193
They are arguing that

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.463
the drone was approaching Crimea

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.966
and that it was operating,

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.067
it was flying without its

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.201
transponders on.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:15.502
And that

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:19.172
prompted the Russians to scramble

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:20.640
the S.U..

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.943
27 jets to intercept it.

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.079
And they, again,

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.014
as you just heard from Oren, said

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:29.849
they did not come in contact,

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.951
they say, with the drone,

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.153
the Russian jets,

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:36.156
and they also did not use their weapons.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:39.292
So we have kind of two narratives here

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.628
for what may have taken place out there.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.264
This will certainly ramp up tensions

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:48.001
in an area that is already beyond tense.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:49.702
I'm standing

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.071
2030 miles away from frontlines

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.574
where Ukrainian and Russian troops

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:56.042
are killing each other

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.777
day in and day out.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.480
And much of the rhetoric, the propaganda

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.648
coming out of Moscow

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.183
right now, out of the state media

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:05.718
is arguing to the Russian audiences

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:06.886
that, hey,

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.721
Russian troops are already

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.890
fighting NATO's and the U.S.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.559
on the ground, even though

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.894
neither organization have sent troops

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:17.397
to engage directly in this terrible war.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:17.864
Yeah.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:19.766
And Phil, at the White House,

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:21.067
officials brief President Biden

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:22.936
about this incident this morning.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.103
Is there any expectation

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:24.871
that President Biden

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.005
might reach out

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.507
to Russian President

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:28.575
Putin to talk about this,

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.476
to try to de-escalate tensions

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:30.810
Yeah, Jake,

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.744
the president was briefed

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:32.579
by national security

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.112
adviser Jake

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.147
Sullivan this morning

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:34.881
about the events

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.583
that transpired over the Black Sea.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:37.917
But there's been no indication

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.252
from White House officials or U.S.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.253
officials writ large

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.688
that the president is considering

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.356
reaching out directly to President Putin.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.857
Now, these two leaders have not spoken

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:45.658
since before

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.627
Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:48.394
And while the president said

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.896
he is open to discussions

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:50.730
with President Putin,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.898
it is only on the grounds

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:52.365
of trying

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.233
to find

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.902
a pathway to end the current conflict.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.370
What you have seen, though,

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.204
there has been obviously

00:03:58.204 --> 00:03:59.572
harsh and sharp language

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.341
Oren laid out in terms of the response.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.009
But there's also been a very methodical

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.711
diplomatic approach here

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.679
in terms of summoning the ambassador

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.214
to the State Department,

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.682
making very clear with the language

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.317
and the statements that they put out,

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.118
their displeasure

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.052
for what transpired

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:13.853
and how they felt like

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.888
this was significantly problematic.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.390
But there has been no sense from U.S.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.091
officials right now

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.292
that there's any desire

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.828
to escalate things any further right now,

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:23.096
just using words

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:23.763
and cautioning

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.798
Russian officials about what happened.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:25.965
All right,

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:26.833
Oren Liebermann, Phil

00:04:26.833 --> 00:04:28.101
Mattingly, Ivan Watson,

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.669
thank you to all of you.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.271
Let's bring in the former secretary

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.972
of defense for Donald Trump, Mark Esper.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.440
Mr. Secretary, good to see you.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.441
Do you agree with the U.S.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:36.009
Air Force's

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.577
assessment that this incident

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:38.177
could lead

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.912
to, quote, unintended escalation?

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:42.081
Well, first of all, it is

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:43.082
certainly reckless,

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.083
and I would say that

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.852
it's certainly intentional.

00:04:45.852 --> 00:04:47.820
The question is, was the intent

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.087
did it

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.088
emanate from the cockpit

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:50.890
or was it directed by somebody

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.125
further up the chain of command?

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:53.192
And yes, indeed,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.361
it could lead to unintentional escalation

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.763
if not controlled.

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.197
You know, during my tenure,

00:04:58.197 --> 00:04:59.132
we had

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.701
similar incidents happen where

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:02.502
Russian aircraft

00:05:02.502 --> 00:05:04.904
would overfly our ships or approach

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.773
very closely our bombers,

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:07.940
but never nothing like this.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.108
So I think it needs to be addressed

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:09.842
very seriously.

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.911
I don't think we should overreact.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:14.213
I suspect right now within the Pentagon

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:15.615
from the chairman of the Joint

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:16.683
Chiefs staff on down,

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:17.350
they are reaching out

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:18.217
to their counterparts

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:20.253
to find out exactly what happened,

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:22.322
to communicate with them and to find what

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:22.922
find out what

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.657
the Russian explanation really is.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.125
And I think that will dictate

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:28.428
in some ways our response not long ago.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:29.429
The State Department

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.730
spokesman, Ned Price, said that

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.098
while he can't speak to Russia's

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.499
intentions, quote,

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.034
the motivations matter much less

00:05:35.034 --> 00:05:36.736
than what actually transpired

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.271
I guess the idea that the Russian jet

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:40.907
was following and, you know,

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.642
playing chicken with this drone

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.210
for 30 to 40 minutes.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:44.944
Do you agree with that?

00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.914
Well, no intentions do matter.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:49.982
I mean, that makes a big difference.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:51.784
But regardless,

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.853
the behavior by the pilots was reckless,

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.255
reckless and unsafe and unprofessional.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.156
They shouldn't be dumping

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.391
fuel on our aircraft.

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.826
That breaks the rules of the road.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:01.594
And I suspect what they were trying to do

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.363
is fly so close

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.530
that the Reaper drone

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.965
would get caught up in jet wash

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.200
and maybe plummet

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.301
into the sea on its own.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:08.968
And they just happened

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.570
to bump into it as well.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.105
All of this is very dangerous behavior.

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:12.438
And again,

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.539
it could lead

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:14.907
to unintentional escalation.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:16.109
That's why I think reaching out

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:17.844
behind the scenes to the Russians

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:18.845
is very important.

00:06:18.845 --> 00:06:19.679
I think we'll know more

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.613
in the next 24 hours.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.615
But we also need to assert publicly

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:23.816
as well as privately that, look,

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.385
we're not going to tolerate this behavior

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.286
because if if you don't do that,

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.287
then you'll see an uptick

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:28.988
from the Russians

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:29.689
against us

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.824
and our allies in the Black Sea region.

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:32.291
And of course,

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:33.960
we are flying in international airspace.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.962
So it's completely unjustified

00:06:36.462 --> 00:06:38.731
The latest CNN poll of Republican

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.066
presidential candidates

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:42.001
has your former boss, President Trump.

00:06:42.001 --> 00:06:42.635
And Florida

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:43.836
Governor Ron DeSantis

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.805
basically neck and neck.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:48.174
DeSantis told Fox News last night

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:50.343
that the war in Ukraine is a, quote,

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.311
territorial dispute.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.547
He said it's not vital to U.S.

00:06:54.547 --> 00:06:55.882
interests. Do you agree

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.951
Well, look, there are only two countries

00:06:58.951 --> 00:06:59.952
in the world that threaten

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.254
the United States existence,

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.855
and that's China and Russia.

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:04.223
And Russia has invaded

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:06.125
a sovereign country.

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.160
Overtaking a large

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.127
chunk of its territory.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:09.762
I do think it's in our vital interests

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:10.797
because,

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:11.364
you know,

00:07:11.364 --> 00:07:12.331
we have to help defend

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:13.433
the democracies of the world.

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.267
We have to push back

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.936
against autocrats like Vladimir Putin.

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:18.137
And if you don't push back,

00:07:18.137 --> 00:07:19.338
that means they'll go elsewhere

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:21.541
and eventually comes home to your shores.

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:22.708
I think the other thing, the reason

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:24.210
why we want to help the Ukrainians

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.211
as well as they are

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.913
knocking down and beating back

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:27.680
the Russian army

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.315
in a way that only helps us.

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:30.817
And at the same time,

00:07:30.817 --> 00:07:32.051
the Western resolve here

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:32.552
with regard

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:34.454
to Moscow sends a clear message

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:35.688
to Beijing

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:37.890
that we will stand up to them as well

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.025
if they decide to

00:07:39.025 --> 00:07:40.460
take action against Taiwan.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:40.626
Well,

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:41.494
what do you make of the fact

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.262
that the two leading candidates

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.064
for president

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:45.932
in the Republican Party

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:46.265
right now

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:47.767
have such a different view

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:48.835
and different assessment

00:07:48.835 --> 00:07:49.669
of this than you do?

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:51.671
I don't know.

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:51.938
I think

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:53.539
you can only chalk it up to politics.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:54.173
I mean, I,

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:55.174
I consider myself

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:56.909
a Reagan Republican and ask myself,

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.344
how would Ronald Reagan approach this?

00:07:58.344 --> 00:07:59.512
And I suspect that

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.279
President Reagan

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.348
would support a young democracy

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:03.683
fighting for its life.

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:05.151
And that's kind of how I look at it,

00:08:05.151 --> 00:08:06.319
the lens through which I look at it.

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:07.787
And I think we as Americans,

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:09.288
the United States, have a responsibility

00:08:09.288 --> 00:08:10.957
to lead the free world.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:11.457
Now, look,

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:12.792
it doesn't mean there are blank checks.

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:14.160
There shouldn't be accountability.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.395
I think we can manage all these things,

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:16.963
but we have to

00:08:16.963 --> 00:08:18.598
we have to abide by our principles

00:08:18.598 --> 00:08:19.899
and live up to our values.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:21.501
Former Secretary of Defense Mark Esper,

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:22.168
thank you so much.

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:23.169
Good to see you again, sir.

